@startuml f9-user-cancel
title F9 — User cancels a task

|Operator|
start
:Click "Cancel" on task in UI;

|UI|
:POST /tasks/:task_id/cancel
 (bearer_token)
 to API Gateway;

|API Gateway|
:Validate bearer_token;
note right
  GW's only logic.
  Auth + route.
end note
:REST POST /cancel
 to Event Router
 { bearer_token, task_id };

|ER|
:Validate bearer_token;
:Read current task state from ER DB;

if (Current state?) then (Queued)
  :UPDATE task SET status=cancelled in ER DB;
  :Persist cancellation event in ER DB;
  :Push to subscribers (GW);
  :Return 200 OK to GW;
  -->[done] "Terminal"
elseif (Preparing) then
  :UPDATE task SET status=cancelling in ER DB;
  :REST POST /control
   to Executor X
   { task_id, action=cancel };
  :EX terminates container;
  :Wait for terminal event from EX;
  :UPDATE task SET status=cancelled in ER DB;
elseif (Running) then
  -->[handoff] "See F7 (action=cancel)";
  :REST POST /control
   to Executor X
   { task_id, action=cancel };
  :EX sends SIGTERM;
  :AG clean shutdown;
  :EX publishes terminal event;
  :UPDATE task SET status=cancelled in ER DB;
else (already terminal)
  :Return 409 Conflict to GW;
  :Log "double cancel" audit;
  stop
endif

|API Gateway|
:Return 200 to UI;

|Operator|
:UI updates task view to "Cancelled";

stop

note right
  From Queued: cancel is synchronous in ER.
  From Preparing/Running: cancel goes through
  ER -> EX -> AG (graceful), then waits for terminal.
  GW just forwards; ER does all the work.
end note

@enduml